@* One line per field that moved: what it is, then how it moved — drawn here for the approval
   screen, the member's table panel and an amended shared object alike, so that a change reads the
   same wherever a reader meets one.

   **A row's detail is drawn part by part, not as two strings around an arrow.** A Power's line is
   a rank, a Source and every Pro and Con on it, and `Before → After` over that printed the whole
   list twice and left the reader to find the three words that differed — the owner's report, on a
   Life Drain with six modifiers. `DiffRow.Parts` says of each part whether it stayed, went,
   arrived or changed form, and each is marked by a *word or a stroke as well as by ink*: a removed
   part is a `<del>`, struck through; an added part is an `<ins>`, in the heading's weight; both
   carry an `sr-only` word, because neither element is reliably announced on its own. Kept parts
   are in `--muted`, so the eye lands on what moved. A one-part row — `Might 6d → 8d` — has one
   changed part and reads exactly as it always did.

   **A whole-row addition or removal says its word once, before the detail**, rather than marking
   every part: "added 4d · Trained · Reach/Throw" is one fact, and six `<ins>`es would be the same
   fact six times. *@

<ul class="diff-rows">
    @foreach (var row in Rows)
    {
        <li>
            <span class="what">@row.What</span>
            <span class="was">
                @if (row.Kind is DiffKind.Added)
                {
                    <span class="verb">added</span>
                    @if (row.After is { } after) { <span class="part">@after</span> }
                }
                else if (row.Kind is DiffKind.Removed)
                {
                    <span class="verb">removed</span>
                    @if (row.Before is { } before) { <span class="part">@before</span> }
                }
                else
                {
                    @foreach (var part in row.Parts)
                    {
                        @switch (part.Kind)
                        {
                            case PartKind.Kept:
                                <span class="part kept">@part.Text</span>
                                break;
                            case PartKind.Added:
                                <ins class="part added"><span class="sr-only">added </span>@part.Text</ins>
                                break;
                            case PartKind.Removed:
                                <del class="part removed"><span class="sr-only">removed </span>@part.Text</del>
                                break;
                            default:
                                <span class="part changed">@part.Was → @part.Text</span>
                                break;
                        }
                        @(" ")
                    }
                }
            </span>
        </li>
    }
</ul>

@code {
    /// <summary>The rows to draw, in the order the diff produced them.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<DiffRow> Rows { get; set; } = [];
}
